ually, the simplest and most robust fix is to only take the first TOKEN match. Let me implement that.\n\nWait, let me re-read the task: \"只取第一个TOKEN类型条目，或根据type字段区分5h和月度配额并显示不同标签\"\n\nThe best approach is to handle both: differentiate by type if possible, but if there are multiple of the same type, only take the first one. Let me look at the actual type values to understand better.\n\nActually, the simplest fix is:\n1. Track if we've already added a token quota\n2. Only add the first one\n\nOr, check the type more specifically. Let me implement a clean solution.\n\nLooking at the code, the issue is clear. The fix:\n- Keep a flag or set to track which quota types we've already added\n- Only add the first TOKEN type entry\n\nHere's my fix:\n\n```python\n# 配额\nquota_data, _ = _query_api(\"/api/monitor/usage/quota/limit\", \"\")\nquotas = []\nseen_token = False\nfor item in quota_data.get(\"limits\", []):\n    t = item.get(\"type\", \"?\")\n    pct = item.get(\"percentage\", 0)\n    cur = item.get(\"currentValue\", 0)\n    total = item.get(\"usage\", \"?\")\n    if \"TOKEN\" in t and not seen_token:\n        seen_token = True\n        quotas.append({\"type\": \"token_5h\", \"percentage\": round(pct, 1), \"current\": cur, \"total\": total, \"label\": \"Token 配额 (5h)\"})\n    elif \"TIME\" in t:\n        quotas.append({\"type\": \"mcp_month\", \"percentage\": round(pct, 1), \"current\": cur, \"total\": total, \"label\": f\"MCP 配额 (月)\"})\n```\n\nThis is clean and simple - just add a `seen_token` flag to only take the first TOKEN entry. Let me implement this.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fef43803-8bda-4097-8d24-a87db3ffa9e8","uuid":"51f73342-9c85-482f-bbc8-edfb56d3f363"}
