{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260523050506429df143eec64d31","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. I need to develop Phase 1 of the match-3 game engine. The project directory exists with just GDD.md. Let me create the task tracking and start implementing.\n\nPhase 1 requirements:\n1. Project initialization (package.json, directory structure)\n2. 8x8 board rendering (HTML5 Canvas, 6 fruit colors)\n3. Touch/mouse swipe swap (adjacent element swap up/down/left/right)\n4. Match detection algorithm (3+ same color horizontal/vertical)\n5. Elimination animation + gravity drop + top fill + chain detection\n6. Special tiles (4-match→striped bomb, 5-match→rainbow, L/T→area bomb)\n7. Move limit + level goals (score target type)\n8. Chain scoring system (chain multiplier: 2-chain 1.5x, 3-chain 2.0x, 4+ 2.5x)\n\nTech requirements:\n- Pure HTML5 Canvas + JavaScript (no framework dependency, package < 4MB)\n- Douyin mini-game compatible\n- Can be tested directly in browser (index.html entry)\n- Clean modular code: Board.js, MatchEngine.js, Renderer.js, InputHandler.js, ScoreSystem.js\n\nLet me create the task list and start implementing. This is a big task but well-defined. Let me break it down and start building.\n\nI'll create the files one by one. Let me structure this:\n\n1. Create directory structure\n2. Create core modules: Board.js, MatchEngine.js, Renderer.js, InputHandler.js, ScoreSystem.js\n3. Create additional modules: Animation.js, Gravity.js\n4. Create main Game.js that ties everything together\n5. Create index.html that works in browser\n6. Test it works\n\nLet me start building all the files. I'll do this efficiently.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef939699-9dac-4e19-a950-f991f68c1f56","uuid":"f2b3ae0b-a6e5-4feb-b2d0-27193d73aa3c"}
